# .mailmap — canonical author/committer identity remapping.
#
# Format (one mapping per line):
#   Canonical Name <canonical-email> <commit-email-to-remap>
#
# Git tools that honor mailmap (git log --use-mailmap, git shortlog -e,
# git blame, GitHub's contributor graph) display the canonical identity
# in place of the commit-time identity. The on-disk commit objects are
# NOT rewritten — this is purely a display affordance.
#
# Why this file exists
# --------------------
# Early v0.1 / v0.2 commits carried a Co-Authored-By: Claude trailer
# from the iteration sessions that bootstrapped the engine. The
# project's no-coauthor-trailer rule was established later, so every
# commit since v0.2.0 is already clean. This mapping consolidates the
# historical Anthropic co-author identity into the canonical maintainer
# identity so GitHub's contributors graph displays 1 contributor
# instead of 2 without requiring a destructive history rewrite.
#
# Secondary mapping: canonicalize the alternate author display name
# ("rlwilliamson-dev") that appears on PR-merge commits authored via
# the GitHub web UI, into the personal-account display name
# ("Ryan Williamson") used on local commits. Both have the same
# privacy email, so GitHub already counts them as one contributor,
# but the mailmap consolidation makes `git log --use-mailmap` and
# `git shortlog -e` show a single consistent name.

# Canonical maintainer identity
Ryan Williamson <123014229+rlwilliamson-dev@users.noreply.github.com> <noreply@anthropic.com>
Ryan Williamson <123014229+rlwilliamson-dev@users.noreply.github.com> rlwilliamson-dev <123014229+rlwilliamson-dev@users.noreply.github.com>
